{"data":{"repository":{"pullRequest":{"reviewThreads":{"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpK0MjAyNi0xMS0yMFQxNDowNjowN1rOugRkxQ=="},"nodes":[{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHgS","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed. At `dc588d2c` GitHub reports the pull request `MERGEABLE`, and `BLOCKED` comes from the review decision alone. `running-legion.md` now differs from its base only by this change's review-bot sentence: main's #4040 paragraph is taken whole (ed157dc9).\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHga","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in d1524729. The page reads `gh pr checks <n>`, says why never `--required`, and the empty-set paragraph now agrees with it. 0c9b16ff makes the rig's route answer `--required` with the required set alone. I read the two reads at this head: `--required` gives 3 rows, the rollup 51.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHge","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in d1524729. Lines 34-43 read the run's own status first. The log read and the re-run wait for `completed`, and a re-run GitHub refuses is recorded and pressed again on the next wake.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHgj","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: go/worker-common.md:14 names the three holders again (the tester in `testing`, the reviewer in `reviewing`, the implementer while it holds `implementing`; the merger and a retro implementer re-run nothing), and roles_test.go pins that list, failing on 4beafeea's text."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHgq","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in d1524729. Line 228 opens the section with its case, a red the one re-run cannot clear, and sends a 5xx, a refusing registry or an ended runner to its one re-run first. So world `c` takes its re-run.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHgv","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: finding-asks.md:24 keeps the condition (the controller acts only when the role found no issue for the test, or one that reads `done`) and asks for no second comment on an occurrence the role posted; the guard's censusFaults pins it, failing on 4beafeea's text."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHgw","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in d1524729: line 94 reads \"One re-run belongs to the head\".\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHgy","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in d1524729: line 306 says the guard pins the merge-queue wording in merge-gate.md, and `worker-skill.test.ts` does pin it there.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHg3","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in d1524729: lines 190-202 give the three ends as a list, and the first-read condition is its own sentence on the second bullet.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHg5","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in d1524729. The page, `findings.md` and `finding-asks.md` all say \"unless it reads `done`\", and a grep of the worker and controller skills finds the old phrase nowhere.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHg7","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in d1524729 and ea7674bf: `core/tester.md:5`, `pr-body.md` and `go/reviewer.md` each name both waits.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHg9","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in 0c9b16ff. Every call holds the flock from its read to its write, and the concurrency rows pin it. This round's review has a new comment on the `counted` rule, which the lock now makes redundant. That comment is a follow-on, not this finding coming back.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHg_","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in 0c9b16ff. `superRefine` refuses a `follows` that names no route, and `worker_world` runs `--check` before any agent boots.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHhC","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in 9535ece2. Each retired sentence is expected at its line, so a pattern that stops matching fails, and the kept sentences are expected to pass. A gap of another shape remains: no pattern refuses a re-run *grant*. It is part of this round's finding on `worker-common.md`.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHhG","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: world.txt is gone, and RedWorld.world is z.enum(RED_WORLDS). Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHhH","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in 8ffbab24: `own_dispatch` calls `run_database_url`, the copy is gone, and rig rows pin the `u?x` case.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHhK","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in 8ffbab24. red_report trims the routes red_fixture marks and publishes through `gh-standin.ts --publish`, so one publisher remains. One follow-on is new in this round: red_report's jq-and-mv of fixtures.json does not take `fixtures.lock`.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHhN","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in 6dbfc761: one `ghCalls`, one parse of each record body, one list of accepted completions and one `earliest()`.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHhP","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in 8ffbab24: `given_omp`, `pinned_command` and `architect_assignment`. One follow-on is new in this round: `pinned_omp` now has one caller, and its error message garbles when `SKILL_SCENARIOS_OMP` is set.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63nHhT","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Fixed in d1524729: `packages/daemon/.changes/unreleased/pr3514-red-at-the-head.yaml` names the five prompt changes.\n\n<!-- legion: {\"session\":\"01a1dde7-b2f0-7190-8b33-0dd34254f9cd\",\"phase\":\"review\",\"head\":\"dc588d2cd29aa5833e4133b481c74eca84b67b6e\"} -->"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSgq","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: concepts.md names the three roles again, with the merger and a retro implementer re-running nothing."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSgv","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: go/reviewer.md:17's order records the failure before the re-run. Accepted. go/reviewer.md:9 has a new finding in round 3: its re-run has no phase condition."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSgx","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: red-at-the-head.md:193-198 names both bounds. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSgz","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: the page is 286 lines, under plan T1's 300, and the merge-queue rule is one sentence under 'Who may re-run'. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSg0","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: a read of the head's CI in the pressing turn counts as a poll (score.ts reread). Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSg2","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: world.txt is no longer written or read; only world.json is checked against the directory. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSg3","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: cmd_run, cmd_batch and red_fixture go through red_world, and the dead arm is gone. Accepted. One more letter-keyed site, red_workflows' case at rig.sh:2892-2903, is in round 3's body."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSg6","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: red_report's read and write run under flock on fixtures.lock. Accepted. Its 12 lines are copied in rerun_settle, a Minor in round 3's body."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSg7","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: counted is gone, and answered is written under the lock on every call. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSg8","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: routes parse as z.looseObject, so unknown keys survive the write. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wSg9","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: standinRun drops every ENVOY_* variable before it runs. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wShB","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: pinned_omp is folded into pinned_command with its own message. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wShF","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: launch keys the process-group path on 'type -P tmux'. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wShH","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: --omp is always a mise spec, and --omp-binary refuses a non-executable path. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wShI","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: finding-asks.md:24's condition is back (\"You act on it when the role found no issue for the test, or found one that reads `done`\"), pinned by censusFaults."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wShJ","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: each budget's record comment begins with its own line (merger.md:66-67, :70). Accepted. Round 3 has a new finding on the same step: the occurrence is posted only after a green group build, which merges the pull request and ends the watch."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wShK","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: services_up builds ./cmd/dispatch once, and start_dispatch has its bound. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds63wShO","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-reviewer"},"body":"Read at 4beafeea: READERS takes jq, python3, node and bun, and the run variable is expanded. Accepted."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGR1","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: the holder list is back in go/worker-common.md:14, the merger and a retro implementer re-running nothing; TestEveryRolePartCarriesItsGuidanceRule (roles_test.go:674) pins it, and its string is absent from 4beafeea's file."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGR7","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: \"takes the head's one re-run first while you hold `reviewing`\", pinned in roles_test.go. The minor, by the architect's ruling: an unreported check (a run of the head holds its failed job, the counted set does not list it yet) is waited for and gets no re-run, while an absent one keeps main's existing re-run; go/reviewer.md:9 and red-at-the-head.md:160 say so, each pinned."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGSC","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: concepts.md names the three roles with the merger excluded, and troubleshooting.md gives the reviewer its limit on a check the base does not require."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGSD","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: the condition is back, a tracked test needs nothing more of the controller, and its own comment is only for an open issue its own search finds that the role did not; pinned by censusFaults."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGSF","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: \"where 0 is carried, 1 is not, and anything else is cannot compare\", pinned in the guard (ANCESTRY_EXIT_STATUSES), absent from 4beafeea's page."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGSM","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: the merger runs the occurrence steps with the record, before the requeue, saying the requeued build's outcome is not yet known, since no step of the merger's after a merge is reachable (the daemon sends it no message for a merge, and the merge closes the issue); pinned in TestTheMergerQueuesAFailedChecksEjectionOnceMore."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGST","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: NO_LANE_IS_RERUN needs the lane noun followed only by helper words before the re-run, and REVIEWER_RERUNS_NOTHING a reviewer subject (or a `you` in a sentence that names a review bot); kept rows for your three sentences pass, and the retired ones are still refused. Every pattern was compared at every match position over 121 Markdown files: the two narrowed ones lose only those cases and gain nothing."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGSY","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: the attempt fact needs a positive integer; row trial-a-head-36 with `\"attempt\": null` fails on the old rule and passes on the new. The batch of record re-scored under it is byte-identical (200 lines), so no row moves."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGSe","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: on the next wake after a refusal the role reads the spend again before it presses, as before the first press."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGSo","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: pi-legion's skills-guard.test.ts holds every fenced bash block and every inline ancestry command of the docs page equal to the page's (`<o>/<r>` as `<owner>/<repo>`), in the package CI selects on both pages; shown failing on a docs copy with one block changed. The run-must-end paragraph now follows the first-line read."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGSx","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8fbc7a68 and b83734b4: `gh-standin.ts`'s top-level script is split into a pure `parseCall(argv, env, read)` (`:614`), which reads each file the call names once into `files`; a pure `answer(call, fixtures, now)` (`:927`), which computes the stamp once (`:950`) and returns what the call prints, its status, whether it writes and the fixtures it leaves; and a `main` of 86 lines (`:1483-1568`; it was 118 at 8fbc7a68, and b83734b4 moves its call recorder into `recorder(run, as, args, at)`). `withoutServices` is exported, so `gh-standin.test.ts` imports it rather than copying the environment filter. 11 of the file's 26 rows now answer through `answer` in-process. The other 15 still spawn the stand-in, one process per call, because each tests what the process does across calls: a route's count across processes and concurrent calls, the lock, a watch's record and frames, the shared-world refusal, and the publish to a listener."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGS4","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8fbc7a68: the `BOUND_WAKES` arm and `bound` are deleted, with the row that hand-wrote its reminder wake (fixture `trial-i-head-127`); the `reread` row (\"a read in the pressing turn stays a poll when a reminder turn follows it\") is kept. `scoreRuns`' three chains are one table, `scenarios` (`score.ts:4341`), whose entries name each scenario's scorer, prefix, sub-runs and stop rule, and `trial` is written once, as `RED_TABLE.run_prefix` from `jq/worlds.json`. `ghMethod` (`score.ts:938`) reads the method from the call's recorded `request`; its argv reading stays only for archived calls recorded before the stand-in kept `request`. The same commit also gives `rerun_pressed` and the scorer one press test, `pressed` in `jq/routes.jq`."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGS-","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: one LANE (and LANE_QUALIFIER) source builds all six noun groups, and prosePinFaults is split into retiredClaimFaults and missingSentenceFaults."}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDORFy7ds66BGTF","isResolved":true,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"legion-implementer"},"body":"Fixed in 8876bbf1: the fragment says \"every phase worker's prompt\" and names the three roles, never the merger."}]}}]}}}}}